 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "nuk and mos",
   "text": "Nuk says that something is not so: nuk e di, \"I don't know\". Mos tells someone not to do something: mos e bëj, \"don't do it\". In fast speech nuk is often just s': s'e di."
  }
